What remo said.

Also, more specifically, in the past when trying to learn larlermorna I've
had trouble when I see old pictures describing the system.  It'd be nice if
there was one well drawn (or even just use paint) description of exactly how
the system works with an example of each letter individually.

Another note for if you decide to write up an official design doc for llm,
lindar:  I think that it would be helpful if you made any examples in the
design doc to be as un-creative as possible.  If someone asks me for an
example of a basic bridi I don't say {lo gerku poi se cinri kei co blabi ku
batci lo simlu be lo ka se prami fi ce'u jai ko'a kei vau}, I say {lo gerku
ku batci lo nanmu}.  The best kind of examples are the kind that describe
the fundamentally important attribute that you are trying to exemplify and
nothing more.

It would be helpful if: AFTER describing llm concretely you could show some
stylistic variations.

